ZEELAND, Mich.


, Oct. 21, 2026


/[PRNewswire](http://www.prnewswire.com/) / -- MillerKnoll, Inc. ("MillerKnoll" or the "Company") (NASDAQ: MLKN), a growth-oriented small-cap value company in the industrial and consumer sectors, announced today its Board of Directors ("Board") has unanimously appointed Jeff Stutz as Chief Executive Officer and a member of the Board, effective immediately. Stutz has served as Interim Chief Executive Officer since June 30, 2026.


"Jeff brings deep institutional knowledge, broad industry experience, and a proven record of leadership at MillerKnoll, and the Board has full confidence in his ability to drive long-term shareholder value," said John R. Hoke III, Chairman of the Board. "As Interim CEO, Jeff has made an immediate and meaningful impact by driving stronger operating income, margins and earnings. Following a rigorous search process, the Board believes Jeff is the right leader for MillerKnoll as we continue to focus on accelerating sales, improving profitability and creating value for our shareholders."


"This is a pivotal time for MillerKnoll, and I am energized by the opportunity to continue working with our talented teams and iconic brands across the Company as we focus on elevating our performance and creating long-term value," said Mr. Stutz. "Serving as Interim CEO over the past few months, I have been working even more closely with our teams, customers and partners around the globe, reinforcing my conviction in our strengths and upside potential. I look forward to partnering with the Board and our teams to sharpen our priorities, manage costs with discipline, strengthen our balance sheet and build on our foundation to deliver for our shareholders, customers and associates."


**About Jeff Stutz**


Mr. Stutz has more than 25 years of leadership experience in the design and manufacturing industry. He served as Chief Operating Officer from September 2025 to June 2026, overseeing the Company's International Contract segment, global manufacturing operations, and European-based brands including HAY, Muuto, Colebrook Bosson Saunders (CBS), and NaughtOne. Previously, he served as Chief Financial Officer for more than 10 years, leading MillerKnoll's global financial operations and helping guide the Company through periods of macroeconomic challenge and opportunistic growth.


Mr. Stutz joined Herman Miller in 2001 and held several finance leadership roles before becoming CFO, including Vice President of Investor Relations, Corporate Treasurer, and Chief Accounting Officer.


He holds a Bachelor's degree in Accounting from Michigan State University and an MBA from Grand Valley State University.


